{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Pass data from child views up to their ancestors.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/preferences"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ImageDecoding"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Preferences","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Protocols","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceKey"],"anchor":"Protocols"},{"title":"Storage","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceValues"],"anchor":"Storage"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit’s preference system enables "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"bottom-up data flow","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the reverse of environment values. While the environment passes data down from parent to child, preferences let child views publish values that ancestors can observe and react to."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The system mirrors SwiftUI’s preference API and consists of three parts:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceKey","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Protocol that defines a named value type with a default and a reduce strategy","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceValues","type":"reference","isActive":true}]},{"type":"text","text":": Type-safe storage that holds all preference values for a scope"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceStorage"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Stack-based collector that manages preference contexts per render pass"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A built-in example is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": a child view sets ","type":"text"},{"code":".navigationTitle(\"Settings\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the enclosing navigation container reads that preference to render the title bar.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Defining a Preference Key","anchor":"Defining-a-Preference-Key"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A preference key declares what type of value it carries and how multiple values from sibling children are combined:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct CounterKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: Int = 0","","    static func reduce(value: inout Int, nextValue: () -> Int) {","        value += nextValue()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"defaultValue","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Returned when no child has set this preference","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(value:nextValue:)"}]},{"text":": Combines values when multiple children set the same key","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" implementation simply takes the last value. Override it when you need additive behavior (summing counts), array collection, or other merge strategies."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Setting a Preference","anchor":"Setting-a-Preference"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Child views publish a preference using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".preference(key:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct ItemView: View {","    var body: some View {","        Text(\"Item\")","            .preference(key: CounterKey.self, value: 1)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Under the hood, this wraps the view in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceModifier"},{"type":"text","text":" that calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preferences.setValue(_:forKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" during rendering. The value is reduced into the current scope using the key’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" function."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Observing Preferences","anchor":"Observing-Preferences"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ancestor views react to collected preferences using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onPreferenceChange(_:perform:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct ItemList: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","        }","        .onPreferenceChange(CounterKey.self) { totalCount in","            \/\/ totalCount == 3 (three children each set value: 1, additive reduce)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier pushes a new preference context, renders all children (which set their preferences), pops the context, and fires the callback with the accumulated result.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Navigation Title Shortcut","anchor":"The-Navigation-Title-Shortcut"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"TUIkit provides ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey"},{"text":" as a built-in preference key with a convenience modifier:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct SettingsPage: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            Text(\"App settings go here\")","        }","        .navigationTitle(\"Settings\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationTitleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" uses the default ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (last value wins), so the deepest child’s title takes precedence.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"How Preferences Flow per Frame","anchor":"How-Preferences-Flow-per-Frame"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Preferences are collected fresh every frame. Here’s the lifecycle within a single render pass:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reset"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RenderLoop.render()"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preferences.beginRenderPass()"},{"type":"text","text":", clearing all callbacks and resetting the stack to a single empty context"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": As the view tree renders top-down, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceModifier"},{"type":"text","text":" views call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setValue(_:forKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which reduces values into the current stack frame"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Scope","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"OnPreferenceChangeModifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pushes a new context before rendering its subtree, isolating child preferences","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Collect","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": After the subtree finishes, the modifier pops the context (merging into the parent) and fires the callback with the scoped result"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discard"}]},{"type":"text","text":": At the start of the next frame, everything resets: stale preferences never persist"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This per-frame reset ensures preferences always reflect the current view tree. Removed views stop contributing automatically.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Reduce Strategies","anchor":"Reduce-Strategies"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function determines how multiple children’s values combine. Common patterns:"}]},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strategy"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Implementation","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use Case"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Last value wins","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"value = nextValue()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (default)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Titles, labels: deepest child wins"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Additive"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"value += nextValue()","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Counting items, summing heights"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Array collection","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gathering menu items, breadcrumbs"}]}]]]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Array collection example","struct BreadcrumbKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: [String] = []","","    static func reduce(value: inout [String], nextValue: () -> [String]) {","        value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit":{"abstract":[{"text":"A declarative, SwiftUI-like framework for building Terminal User Interfaces in Swift.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit","kind":"symbol","title":"TUIkit","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"tuikit-logo.png"},{"type":"card","identifier":"tuikit-logo.png"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/CustomViews":{"role":"collectionGroup","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build your own views by composing existing ones or creating custom view modifiers."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/customviews","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documen